  "body": "Stacked on #1817 (merge #1817 first)\n\n## What changed\n\n2D rest machining now accepts Zigzag. It cuts rows, then closes each rest boundary to clear wall cusps.\n\nRows use an inset of `min(0.01 mm, stepover / 4)`. This prevents numeric boundary crossings without removing interior rows from small pockets.\n\nThe existing plain-pocket row algorithm moves unchanged to `pocket_zigzag.rs`. `pocket.rs` stays at 398 lines. No dependency is added.\n\nThe MCP skill now describes Zigzag support. Adaptive still has its named refusal. The entered previous tool remains an explicit trust assumption.\n\nThe remaining #1490 work has separate issues: Adaptive #2031, entry from cleared space #2032, and previous-operation stock #2033.\n\n## Cause\n\nRows alone leave cusps at the rest boundary. A closing pass clears them. Rows that touch the boundary can cross it through numeric rounding.\n\nA fixed 0.01 mm inset removes all rows from a tiny pocket. The stepover cap preserves those rows.\n\nThe geometry follows this project's existing scan and offset routines. See Held's [Zigzag Pocket Machining](https://www.cosy.sbg.ac.at/~held/projects/pocket_zig/pocket.html) and [pocket geometry monograph](https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/3-540-54103-9). [Yao, Gupta and Nau](https://www.cs.umd.edu/~nau/papers/yao2003algorithms.pdf) provide the cutter-coverage context. The inset and closing-pass choices are ours.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `zigzag_rest_covers_corner_residue_without_gouges_or_unsafe_rapids`: red at the original refusal. Green after the fix. Covers both directions and 1.5/4 mm steps.\n- `tiny_rest_pocket_keeps_interior_rows_when_previous_tool_fits_nowhere`: red with the fixed inset. Green with the stepover cap.\n- Expected-change tests now accept Zigzag at the motion and operation parameter doors.\n- Closing-pass mutation: red coverage; restored green. The first fixture left 287 measured residue points uncut.\n- Zero-inset mutation: red verifier, with six crossings; restored green.\n- Fixed-inset mutation: red tiny-pocket center coverage; restored green.\n- Old `upstream/main` pocket code: red; restored green.\n- Old `base-1817` rest strategy: red refusal; restored green. The parent baseline supplies the export absent from `upstream/main`.\n\nThe requested `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed all three steps in 34.4 minutes before the inset cap.\n\nAfter the cap, `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main --only motion` passed its affected motion step in 663 seconds.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed on the final code.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone from #1490. The diff against `base-1817` changes no `.nc` or `.cl` file.\n\nThe two-dot diff against `upstream/main` lists 147 files. All were checked against the merge base and parent.\nOf these, 146 exactly reverse upstream changes absent from the older parent branch. The other is #1817's unchanged `pocket_rest_corners.cl` addition.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nNo real machine was used. This change does not implement new Adaptive paths, cleared-space entry, or previous-operation stock input.\nThose features require separate depth and cutter-clearance proofs in #2031, #2032, and #2033.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #1817 changes `rest_pocket`, `rest_strategy`, and the expected-refusal tests. This branch stacks on its head.\n- #2013 and #1954 touch the same file, different module declarations in `machining2d/mod.rs`; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #1738 touches the same file, a different section of the MCP skill; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/1490-rest-strategies.md`.\n\nChangelog: 2D rest Zigzag clears wall cusps with closing passes and preserves interior rows in small pockets.\n\nProcess change: yes\n\nEffort: max\n\nFixes #1490\n\n## UI images\n\nPocket Passes before this PR (`a49322b9`):\n\n![Pocket Passes before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-2037/before-pocket-passes.png)\n\nPocket Passes at the reviewed head (`9c4d732`):\n\n![Pocket Passes after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/pr-screenshots/pr-2037/after-pocket-passes.png)\n\nBoth captures use the same shell fixture and actual egui rendering. The controls are visually unchanged; the UI source change preserves the rest field.\n",
